<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.00%" pitch="-2.00%">
            Take a slow breath in.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And let it go.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Let your body settle. Let your hands rest. Let the day behind you begin to loosen its hold.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            You are here now. And here is safe.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Tonight we open the book of Isaiah.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            And what we find there is not a lecture. Not a warning. Not a list of things you still need to do.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            What we find there is a voice — direct, personal, unhurried — speaking words that were meant to reach you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Fear not.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Those two words appear again and again in Isaiah. God says them like He means them. Like He knows what it is to carry fear. Like He has seen it in His people across every generation, and He keeps coming back with the same answer.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Fear not, for I am with you.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Fear not, for I have called you by name.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Fear not, for you are mine.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            These are not reassurances from a distance. They are not words tossed over a wall. They are the words of a God who draws near. Who enters the waters with you. Who walks beside you through the difficult places.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Tonight, let those words do their work.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Let them move past the noise and into the places where fear has taken up residence.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Breathe again. Slow and easy.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Fear not. God is with you. You are called by name. You are precious. You are held. You can rest.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
